{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/962857-ic-a-cycle-unending","id":962857,"title":"[IC]A Cycle Unending","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-03T09:54:27-07:00","id":962857,"title":"[IC]A Cycle Unending","content":"All of you receive messages from your elders telling you to be at Blackness Castle just east of Edinburgh for a meeting the evening of 2 January 2016. It is an old castle that for the most part stands empty. You are going there to meet a William Dunsirn and you are all warned that he is not to be trifled with. Wallace recalls meeting William once at a large family gathering, he is slightly shorter than average but covered in muscle. When he talks you can tell that he is a man of deep cunning.<br /> <br /> When you get to the Castle it is cold and rather dark out. A light dusting of snow has covered everything and it looks like it will snow later in the night. As you enter the Castle you are greeted by a rather large man that looks like he is better suited to threatening people than skulking about in an old castle. <b>&quot;The master is occupied for a few moments if you would wait here for a few moments he will be with you shortly.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> The three players find themselves together for the first time with a few minutes before they meet William.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T12:27:15-07:00","id":962944,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul, dressed in an old-fashioned winter coat and a hat, brushed off the last bits of snow from his figure. &quot;Damnation!&quot; he thought to himself. &quot;How am I supposed to work or feed in this unwelcoming climate?&quot;. Regaining his composure he turned to the other guests in this dark castle, as if noticing them for the first time.<br /> &quot;Greetings, gentlemen&quot; he said in a reserved, subtly friendly voice. &quot;I am Raul Abrantes, a physician by trade and a philosopher, at your service. Do you, by any chance, know the specifics of why our kind host wanted to see us? Or maybe you have even met mister Dunsirn?&quot;<br /> <br /> Raul extends his hand in a greeting gesture, waiting for his newly met comrades to do the same. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T19:20:47-07:00","id":963042,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William finishes up some business on his phone before returning it to his pocket as he enters. He takes brief note of the muscle as he steps into the building proper, but pays the servant little mind. As he approaches the gathered group they can see William is dressed in a tailored long wool overcoat making it difficult to make out the clothing underneath. There is still a light dusting of snow on his shoulders, and it causes the paleness of his skin to stand out even more. <br /> <br /> He shakes the hand offered, <b>&quot;Evening, William St. John, unfortunately I was not provided with an itinerary for the meeting or its purpose. Most of my business tends to be focused around London so I rarely end up this far north so I have not had the chance to meet Mr. Dunsirn before.&quot; </b>William looks around the room in the castle for a moment, <b>&quot;Although given our host's choice of meeting location I think we can assume this is not merely a simple business meeting.&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T07:20:52-07:00","id":963208,"title":"","content":"Wallace Dunsirn<br /> <br /> Greetings, greetings,my good men! I'm Walace Dunsirn, a pleasure to make your acquaintance, gentlemen.-he is wearing a tailor-made three pieces suit and rest part of his considerable weighth in a sturdy-looking cane. He smiles and pats his big belly before shaking your hand, vigorously-&quot;I do hope that there's more than bussiness, but I am as less informed as you are, I'm afraid. I do know cousin William, he is a rather... intense man. You'll see. Whatever it is the reason he has to bring us here tonight I'm sure will be way worth the trouble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T12:46:47-07:00","id":963338,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul smiles and nods. &quot;Ach, so you are both Europeans, then? Wonderful. I, for one, hail from Mexico, from the Pisanob branch of the Family.&quot; He glances over the hall to see if the steward is about to return. If not approached he intends to stay silent, instead focusing on bringing up any potentially useful background details about the Dunsirn family and the city of Edinburgh. What, again, was the Prince's name? The Sherriff's? Are there any recent events, conflicts or places of particular significance? Besides the residents of this castle is there any other Giovanni presence to speak of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:10:53-07:00","id":964602,"title":"","content":"After you make your brief introductions, the man you are here to meet steps out of another room.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Sorry I kept you waiting, some scum was sending my phone messages about how to become a secret, silent ninja shopper or some such nonsense. One of my people just tracked him down. It would appear that his extended family has suffered from a series of unrelated financial mishaps. Apparently they are serious enough that his grandfather is getting kicked out of the nice home they had him in and he is probably faring the best of any of them. Anyway where was I, yes, now I remember. What can any of you tell me about Lord Camden, once Seneschal to Mithras, Prince of London?&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T09:50:17-07:00","id":965015,"title":"","content":"&quot;Other than he is deader than a tombstone, not much, really&quot; - he excuses himself with his right hand over his chest and a gentle bow - &quot;... and that he was a Cappadocian, of course&quot; - he adds a second later, not sure if such a well know fact is of any interest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T12:52:25-07:00","id":965201,"title":"","content":"[OOC Notes: Being from the London area I'll assume I have a bit more information, if anything is too much feel free to edit it down as appropriate. Also before the game started I forgot how you wanted to handle dice rolling]<br /> <br /> William St. John<br /> <br /> William looks over the man in front of him, trying to get his measure. <b>&quot;Such delays are understandable. As for Lord Thomas Beckett Camden, I'm afraid my information is spotty at best. What I do know is he was a Cappadocian who served as Mithras's Seneschal for a long period, and was even trusted enough to act as his representative to the founders of the Camarilla. From what I've heard he was killed sometime in the early 16th century by the Giovanni, and Mithras's rage at his death made it very difficult for the family in London for some time after. Things have improved since the ascension of 'Queen' Anne Bowesley, but she is a driven woman who brooks little dissent so we must still tread carefully. &quot; </b>William gives the older Dunsirn a wary and quizzical look. <b>&quot;The question I would ask in return is why do you want to know, what do you gain from this information?&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T04:51:13-07:00","id":965599,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> &quot;The seneschal of Mithras himself, you say?&quot; asked Raul, adding precious little curiosity to that question &quot;I came across that name a couple times during my research. It turns out that he was quite the accomplished historian and necromancer, with some insight into the matters of the departed. Not very much has remained of his work, I'm afraid, yet there are rumors of him having a childe, a figure even more elusive than he was.&quot; The interest his host showed in the long dead vampire concerned Raul greatly, so he nodded approvingly when William asked about the motive of such a question.<br /> <br /> [OOC note: the background info I mentioned in my previous post is really something I'd like to know, unless of course I am straight off my plane to Birmingham and have no way of knowing that]<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T14:04:44-07:00","id":965858,"title":"","content":"[ooc]The Dunsirn have extensive holdings in and around the city and probably about 6 of the blood. But officially the city is run by the Camarillia, the prince is a Toreador named Cameron De Pris and his sheriff is a Brujah named Ducan Blackfist, Camarillia population is about a dozen.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, I recommend that everyone subscribes to this topic if they haven't already. It should help people realize that updates have been posted by someone and keep things moving better.[/ooc]<br /> <br /> You see a small, knowing smile on William Dunsirn's face at the mention of mithras' replacement.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Good, I see why you were the ones sent to me. I will not have to spend time explaining the importance of what I am about to tell you. I have been contacted by a Nosferateu who claims to have found a previously unknown haven that belonged to Lord Camden that has sat untouched since his death. I have no reason to believe that the family is the only interested party in this information, so it seemed prudent to send a group that was able to take care of themselves to investigate. A meeting has been set up with the information broker for 3 nights from now in Nottingham, it will take place in Church rock cemetery, in the largest mausoleum. This knowledge cannot be allowed to spread, find the location of this haven and remove all others who know it's location. Report to me and only me when it is done. Are there any questions?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> He then gives you his contact information and a briefcase full of money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","user":"Browman","date":". 09-08-2016, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T23:34:02-07:00","id":966082,"title":"","content":"Wallace is quick to take the money with his big, greedy hands-&quot;So, we have to meet this Nosferatu, find the haven, destroy any oposition and report back to you&quot;-he caresses the briefcase, smiling-&quot;You can consider it done, cousin. Perhaps you have any suspicions of what we could find in that haven?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T02:53:26-07:00","id":966123,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William takes the briefcase, although he has a slight look of concern on his face. <b>&quot;If this Nosferatu contacted us regarding this information its almost a guarantee he has sought other buyers for this information. I wont be surprised if we aren't the only ones who show up to this meeting. If we are lucky the other interested parties will be too self-interested to share the information about the meeting.&quot; </b>He stops and thinks for a long moment. <b>&quot;Most likely candidates to be interested in such information are other blood mages such as the Tremere. If Lord Camden was the necromancer you say he is Mr. Abrantes, it's likely all sorts of valuable insights could lie within. Necromantic notes, ritual tools and items, if we are lucky perhaps an entire occult library.&quot;</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T14:41:19-07:00","id":966444,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I think we can safely assume that the range of possible buyers for this information is far wider than just blood mages. The local Camarilla and Sabbat would surely be interested in it, too, if not for the power within, then for its value as a bargaining chip in dealings with... well, with us. Add to that mortal users of magic and, obviously, the Nosferatu themselves. These sewer rats play the long game and understand the concept of dividing and conquering. Not to mention there are others creatures of the night, with unfathomable goals&quot; He starts to pace around the chamber, lost in his thoughts for a moment &quot;No matter. We will use the local ghosts to devise a plan, and any further contacts you could provide us, mister Dunsirn, would be of tremendous assistance. And, oh, does this Nosferatu have a name?&quot;<br /> <br /> He turns to his companions and says: Well, if any of you, fine gentlemen, has any ideas as to the approach we should take, then maybe we can discuss this... elsewhere. And if our host would be so kind to provide us with a resting place, then I suggest we may retire there afterwards and leave tommorow night.&quot; He falls silent, waiting for his comrades' response.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T16:58:44-07:00","id":967609,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;Studies into the nature of death, Lord Camden was a master of the lost arts of Mortis. The Nosferatu contact gave his name as Gord, he is likely a middle man as my sources say that they only kindred named Gord they can find is a 13th gen embraced at the turn of century. Hardly the one to find such a treasure. You will find rooms below that do not appear on any records, they even have modern communications.&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T23:58:09-07:00","id":967798,"title":"","content":"&quot;I see...&quot;-he smiles at the description-&quot;Maybe I can finally learn something about that, I must admit I have avoided the more mystical side of our trade for maybe too long. I am a practical man&quot;- He then turns to Abrantes-&quot;Our aproach will depend. Some, we can overbid, others may require a more direct, physical aproach. Is difficult to know without much information about the other interested parties. Gathering that information should be our prime concern&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T01:34:36-07:00","id":968414,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William turns to Raul, <b>&quot;Luckily for us the meeting is in a cemetery, there are likely plenty of spirits we can put to use. I agree that we should leave tomorrow, the sooner we arrive in Nottingham the more time we have to gather information. When we get there we might be able to glean some information about other possible buyers by looking into new arrivals. Perhaps the locals can be persuaded to provide additional information on this Gord which could lead to information about who he is acting as middleman for. Any other thoughts gentlemen?&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-13T03:18:14-07:00","id":968436,"title":"","content":"&quot;I think that settles things for now. Any of you gentlemen could use a refreshment, perhaps? Otherwise we could consider this meeting done and start planning things for tomorrow&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T09:23:15-07:00","id":969978,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;As I said there are accommodations here that you can use, they even have secure communications if you need to reach anyone. I am not sure that you want to explain your presence in Edinburgh to the prince there.&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T12:52:03-07:00","id":972662,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul nods and says &quot;Yes, I think no additional conclusions are needed for now. Do you mind, gentlemen, if I book a train ride to Nottingham and a resting place for tomorrow?&quot; If not met with objections, he adds &quot;Then it's settled. If you excuse me, I had a long journey from America and require some rest&quot;.<br /> <br /> He doesn't, however, go to his room immediately. Instead, his forst stop is a library, where he stays for a while, reading and searching for any topic that seems of particular interest to his host. Then he uses this &quot;secure communication&quot; channel to send a message to his sire:<br /> <br /> &quot;Dunsirn is looking for a haven of Thomas Camden, a fabled Necromancer with obscure ties to the Giovanni. Contacted a neonate Nosferatu in Nottingham and scheduled a meeting there in three nights. He sent us - me, and one member of St. John and his own family each - to conclude the deal. I will write if I learn anything more and do my best to ensure a fair part of knowledge stored in the pursued location finds its way to our vaults. Until then, any information on this &quot;Camden&quot; might prove extremely useful.<br /> <br /> Yours,<br /> R.A.&quot;<br /> <br /> He doesn't expect an answer right away, possibly in two or even three nights. With this thought, and having completed all formalities regarding transportation and accomodation in Nottingham, he falls into daysleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:05:00-07:00","id":972703,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> Addressing the elder Dunsirn, <b>&quot;Very well its not as if we have any intention of remaining here for any length of time as it stands now.&quot; </b>Turning back to the assembled group. <b>&quot;I agree with Mr. Abrantes, I cannot think of any other conclusions we can reach here. Until we get to Nottingham our information is limited, so I will see you on the morrow.&quot; </b>William heads to the accommodations and spends the rest of the evening going over the exchanges since this endeavor may require some expensive tools depending on how this meeting goes, and a little extra capital would be very useful. At the end of the evening he drifts into slumber, dreaming of the various secrets that could lie within the crypt of such an ancient necromancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T10:13:17-07:00","id":973208,"title":"","content":"Just before you leave the next day, the servant of the Dunsirn elder stops you. <b>&quot;Mr Dunsirn wished yo inform you that another will meet you in Nottingham. Mr Rosselini will be fully briefed before you arrive.&quot;</b> the servant gives you a phone number to contact him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:22:19-07:00","id":973938,"title":"","content":"The train ride to Nottingham takes a good portion of night. On route you receive a text from the number for the fourth member of the team. <b>&quot;will meet at train station.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> The train ride is uneventful and the train is basically empty.<br /> <br /> The station in Nottingham is basically completely empty when you arrive. There is a well dressed man leaning against the side of the main building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:12:08-07:00","id":973965,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul is noticeably nervous about how empty and quiet the station is. Might be an ambush. Might be nothing. And there was this Rosselini fellow: could it be the man standing before them? Ultimately, he decided to take a moment to look for any threats lurking in the dark, be it an inanimate trap or an attacker from the shadows.*<br /> <br /> If nothing suspicious presents itself, he approaches the well-dressed man and says:<br /> - Good evening, my friend. Are you looking for something... or someone?<br /> <br /> *[An OOC Note: not sure if this whole &quot;spotting an ambush&quot; thing requires a roll. so I didn't make one, plus you never said how will we resolve such situations]<br /> <br /> [Edit: A <a href=\"http://www.charactersheet.net/rpg/dice-roller/57e2eb58-4430-44f0-aac9-2024adecb046\" target=\"_blank\">roll</a> was made, scoring 1 success]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 09-21-2016, 04:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:22:48-07:00","id":973968,"title":"","content":"For dice rolling everyone should just do their own rolling and post the results. The only people that suffer if you cheat is you.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for an ambush make a perception alertness roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T14:03:27-07:00","id":974017,"title":"","content":"Wallace walks directly to the well dressed man standing in the otherwise empty train station with a speed incongruent with his considerable mass. -&quot;Mr. Rossellini, I presume?&quot;- he tends a big, fat hand to the man as greeting.- &quot;I am Wallace Dunsirn, and these gentlemen here are Mr. Raul Abrantes and Mr. William St. John. We weren't said much about yourself, Mr Rossellini, are you also part of the family?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:39:30-07:00","id":974105,"title":"","content":"-<i>Noticing the train's arrival, Aflie pushes off the wall, checks his cuffs and ring as he walks towards the exiting doors, having been briefed to meet the 3 individuals he had been told about</i>-<br /> <br /> -<i>He stops a agreeable, non-threatening distance away from the group and gives a curt nod with a smile on his face, responding to the one known as Raul Abrantes</i>-<br /> <br /> -<i>Standing before you all, is well dressed, fashion-sensible rather attractive man, with a permanent even tan, as if hed been somewhere abroad before his embrace, and leaving his wavy blond hair golden against his skin. His eyes are remarkable for what appear to be large pupils, but are actually grey sclera instead of normal white. You notice, almost purposely the signet ring of the <u>Rossellini</u> family that he wears</i>-<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>Indeed, good sir! I am looking for someone's to be exact, and it looks by the descriptions, that I have found them...</b>&quot; -<i>He says as he extends his hand, in a gesture of good faith</i>.-<br /> <br /> -<i>Looking over at the rather large fellow who towers over him, responding to his query he simply smiles, winks a single eye and points a 'Bullseye' gesture to Wallace...-</i><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;You got it, Mr. Dunsirn, unfortunately that seems par for the course on both our parts... The powers that be have told me little of yourselves, other than to expect three dapper and proper looking gents at this station, at this rough exact time&quot;</b> <i>-He gestures with etiqeutte looking at his nice Swiss watch, while shaking or not shaking Raul's hand, if it was accepted, should it not be accepted, he switches to Wallace for the handshake, or whoever accepts it-</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T22:41:06-07:00","id":974245,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William takes the hand offered and shakes it. The two things you notice are that he is incredibly pale, and his hand is cool to the touch, both of which unnaturally so. <b>&quot;William St. John, I believe we can get better acquainted as we discuss our business when we get settled.&quot; </b>William steps aside to let anyone else greet the man, and he addresses the group. <b>&quot;I took the liberty of renting a few adjoining rooms at the Park Hotel Nottingham which is roughly 1 km (half mile) from the Church Rock Cemetery.&quot; </b>He pulls out his phone and looks up something up. <b>&quot;Excellent the rooms I have rented are ready, if any of you should need a place to stay, I've rented enough rooms for all of us in case our work precluded us from returning to other accommodations within a reasonable time.&quot; </b>William then waits to see what else anyone has to say as well as if they take him up on his offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:26:11-07:00","id":974427,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul accepts the handshake of the well-dressed man and says:<br /> -Well met, mister Rosselini. Are you from around these parts, by any chance? Oh, and... I don't think I caught your name.<br /> <br /> Noticing the stranger's black eyes Raul did his best to appear unmoved, although he is not certain if he had succeeded. He couldn't shake the feeling that someone is one step ahead of them and that trouble is afoot. Regardless, he decided to remain calm and, as William mentioned the rented rooms, he replied:<br /> - A good idea. We should retire to our rooms and plan our course of action there. We are too exposed here for my taste.<br /> <br /> Saying that, Raul began looking for a cab or any other means of low-profile transportation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T16:40:49-07:00","id":975270,"title":"","content":"Introductions made, the group gets a pair of cabs to the hotel. It is hardly a great place, but it will do for a few nights. You still have a couple hours before sunrise.<br /> <br /> In case it matters, the local &quot;Prince&quot;, Bartholomew Bates, holds court every Thursday night at Propaganda. Visitors passing through are supposed to check in with his sheriff/ seneschal/ second in command Roger Stevens an hour after dark the first full night they are in town at the same location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T14:29:41-07:00","id":976100,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul places a suitcase containing his personal belongings in one of the rooms, looks over everyone present and begins to speak in a fashion that can only be compared to a coach, addressing his team just before the game starts. Only that the other vampires are hardly &quot;his&quot; and hardly a &quot;team&quot; just yet. He chose to wave that away, hoping this will not turn into a leadership contest.<br /> <br /> - So, my fellow conspirators... it seems that now, away form prying eyes we can discuss what exactly are we planning to do in the coming nights. I, for one, am going to visit the cemetery in which we are to meet our contact and get the feel of the place, perhaps even ask the local denizens a question or two. Tomorrow night, I suggest we carouse at least a little in the Prince's court, as is customary in this domain - the last thing that we want is an overzealous Sheriff breathing down our necks because we didn't observe some obscure tradition. Additionally, we could wrangle some information from the other Cainites there and see what are the poilitics all about in this city, as dull as this may be. I get the feeling we will be staying here for a while. With that in mind, I also plan to seek out the local community of mortal occultists... however misguided, they may possess some useful information or provide assistance. If nothing else, they could serve as vessels to gains sustenance from. I am ready to take your suggestions, gentlement. Let's make these nights count.<br /> <br /> He finishes with a smile, waiting for response from his companions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T11:47:48-07:00","id":976639,"title":"","content":"Alfie Rossellini<br /> <br /> ((OOC: MIssed the introduction as I was in Las Vegas for a wedding until last night, only had phone access and wouldnt have been able to properly format my postings, I do apologize.<br /> He would have introduced himself as Alfie Rossellini upon request.))<br /> <br /> -He sets his suitcase and carry on down in one of the rooms, then walks over to the one room everyone is gathered in, and listens to suggestions, opinions and various thoughts and ideas.-<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;While I wont be digging any graves this time around unless its absolutely neccessary&quot; -</b><i>He nods to Raul.-</i> <b>&quot;I do have a vested interest to keep below the Sherriff's and by proxy the Prince's radar, so making an appearance at court is a must. I could look up the Church Rock Cemetary through my contacts, possibly get the updated layout of the Church itself including all known egress and ingress points should it be necessary.&quot;</b> <i>-He shrugs while spinning his watch around to proper positioning as it seems slightly loose on his wrist.-</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T12:14:47-07:00","id":976653,"title":"","content":"&quot;Iwill let the dealing with the dead to our more skilled partners&quot; - Wallace aproaches mr. Rosellini a little too much- &quot;On the other hand I would totally love to make some new acquaintances among the fine kindred of this city, maybe even some business oportunities presents themselves while we carouse our way to some information&quot; - he smiles and slowly licks his lips like he tasted a nice meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T20:43:11-07:00","id":976921,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Presenting ourselves to the Prince seems a wise decision I would rather not have the Prince's forces looking into us while we are trying to take care of our business. I would also very much like to investigate the cemetery itself before the meeting. I'm curious to what I will see on the other side of the Shroud and with any luck I'll find ghosts I can question, perhaps they will have information we can use to our advantage.&quot; </b><br /> <br /> He takes a seat and holds his hand pensively under his chin and regards Wallace. <b>&quot;You bring up an interesting point Mr. Dunsirn, none of us really know what sort of abilities we have available. While I understand anyone's desire for secrecy, figuring out what vampiric gifts we have available will make leveraging those assets much easier. I myself had reached a level of ability along the Ash Path where I can see, speak to, and physically interact with things along the other side of the Shroud; hence my interest in examining the cemetery grounds itself.&quot; </b>He then waits to see if anyone else offers any information on what blood powers they have which might be of use, although his posture makes it clear that he is not pressing the point but rather is placing forth an idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T23:25:45-07:00","id":977006,"title":"","content":"(OOC Flavor Text for his text RP: <br /> <br /> <i><b>(Eyes of Shadow</b></i> (as a 2pt Merit)<br /> There is something about your eyes that makes you look dark and dangerous. Making eye contact with you is like staring into the Abyss. It may not be obvious why, but anyone you talk to gets a chill when they meet your gaze. The difficulty for any Intimidation roll is reduced by the number of points in this Merit (to a minimum of 2) ((Difficulty of 4 instead of 6 for rolls involving intimidation))<br /> <br /> <b><i>(Clan Friendship: Giovanni</i></b> (4pt. Merit)<br /> One particular Clan (GIOVANNI) (not your own) has a special liking for you. You might have done the Clan as a whole a favor at some point, or perhaps you\u2019re just a loud voice in support of their aims. Whatever the case, you\u2019re at -2 difficulty on all friendly Social rolls involving members of the Clan in question.) ((So in this case, members of Clan Giovanni tend to look very favorably on Alfie, not sure if this also includes the other PCs))<br /> <br /> ( <i><b>\u2022 Shadow Play)</b></i><br /> (This power grants the vampire limited control over shadows and other ambient darkness. Though the vampire cannot truly \u201ccreate\u201d darkness, she can overlap and stretch existing shadows, creating patches of gloom. This power also allows Kindred to separate shadows from their casting bodies and even shape darkness into the shadows of things that are not there.<br /> Once a Kindred takes control of darkness or shadow, it gains a mystical tangibility. By varying accounts cold or hellishly hot and cloying, the darkness may be used to aggravate or even smother victims. Certain callous Lasombra claim to have choked mortals to death with their own shadows.<br /> <u><i>System</i></u>: This power requires no roll, but a blood point must be spent to activate it. Shadow Play lasts for one scene and requires no active concentration. Kindred cloaking themselves in shadow gain an extra die in their Stealth dice pools and add one to the difficulties of ranged weapon attacks against them. <u>Vampires who use the darkness to make themselves more terrifying add one die to Intimidation dice pools.</u> Opponents plagued by flapping shadows and strangling darkness subtract one die from all Stamina dice pools (including soak). Mortals, ghouls, and other air-breathers reduced to zero Stamina by strangling shadows begin to asphyxiate; vampires lose all appropriate dice but are otherwise unaffected. Only one target or subject may be affected by this power at any given time, though some modicum of concealment is offered to a relatively motionless group.)<br /> <br /> <i>-He looks towards the ever-enclosing Wallace making eye contact as he approaches, letting his eyes <b>darken</b> as do the <b>shadows</b> that seem to envelop him as Dunsirn gets just a little too close, increasing intensity the closer he gets- <br /> <br /> ((OOC<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />AS A PLAYER, IF <u>NECESSARY</u>, though I am not into the whole player versus player rolling thing in any aspect. However this is how Aflie would react to the giant of a man he hardly knows encroaching his personal bubble if it were, lol) <u><b><a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Roller Used</a></b></u></i><br /> <u><b>Aflie Rossellini rolls 8 dice to Intimidation : Casual Subtle Threat (Diff 4) 4,2,2,3,4, 8,10,5,6 [6 successes]) =/intent = (Show of Strength/Keep your distance, or back off))</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Id suggest splitting up, but in times like these with the situation as is... perhaps all of us presenting ourselves to the Sheriff and Prince, would be ideal. Having two of us 'digging holes' and the other two making an appearance at court would look rather suspicious if caught red-handed. However, it does bring a certain plausible deniability, I, for one am not for the latter idea. Lets keep the group together is my opinion. Then once introductions are done, we can go about other aspects.&quot; </b><br /> <br /> <i>-He shrugs, casually looking to each of the members, then upon hearing William's second statement he nods-</i><br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Fair play to the group, and good use of information should we all know what each other is capable of... I am quite capable at social situations both hostile and friendly, when you look this good it should come with the territory, no? Some would call me a 'Intrusion Specialist' or as the old timers call it, Breaking and Entering... Evading Security devices, picking locks, cracking safes, and preventing others from doing the same... I am also quite capable at never being notice, or shadowing people if necessary, I dabble in the arts of the Shadow, coercing and conditioning the minds of others, also fairly capable of dealing with things in a physical manner, though not nearly as capable as Mr. Dunsirn here.<br /> <br /> -</b>He tilts his head and nods to Wallace with respect to his overt Strength-<br /> <br /> <b>When all else fails...While I may not have the ability to talk to ghosts or see' em, I am quite capable at making them&quot; </b><br /> <br /> <i>-He lifts his vest, revealing his holstered pistol and flashes a smile-</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T23:30:24-07:00","id":977010,"title":"","content":"-&quot;I suppose at this point everybody knows that my particular branch of the family is infamous for not worrying too much about the soul economy. We are very pragmatic people without time for mysticisms of any sort. Plus I consider playing with your food to be bad table manners. I had focused myself on the particular gifts of our blood that lets me crush my oposition, be it his will or his bones.&quot;-he reinforces his statement clenching his enormous fist and smiling widely. He looks to Rosselliny and his smile freezes in his face. He coughs twice and take a couple of steps back, giving the new member of the group some space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  Added reaction to Rosellini 09-27-2016, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T01:50:01-07:00","id":977073,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> - A fair point, mister St. John. I, for one, used to be an accomplished doctor and biologist, and there is hardly any life form I cannot describe or heal, as well as not many conditions I cannot esamine. Other than that, I hope it is not too vain if I say that if there is a sorce of occult knowledge worth trying, I have tried it. Several times over. My research has also made me highly attuned to the presence of supernatural and mundane phenomena. And this &quot;mad necromancer&quot; look scares people pretty good, too - he adds, with a wry smile.<br /> After a moment, he continues:<br /> - As to the more mystical abilities of our kind, thanks to my practice in the Black Art, I am capable of seeing, summoning and compelling to service ghosts residing on our side of the Shroud. Also, if you need any menial labor done quickly, corpses I raise from their graves will attend to the task. With any luck, I will soon be able to make them fight on our side, too.<br /> <br /> He finishes, evidently content with his portfolio. Although he had noticed that shadows in the room have shifted, he decided not to point this out, as this &quot;Alfie&quot; clearly can stand his ground. Very strange, however. He wondered, what vampiric power could produce such an effect, as it wasn't any of the signature Disciplines of his clan - of that, he was sure. Gaining his composure, he adds:<br /> <br /> - Then we have no secrets towards each other anymore. Mister. St. John, if you share my desire to scout the Church Rock Cemetery, then I suggest we go now and make advantage of whatever is left of the night, hm?<br /> <br /> He waits for a response, however unless someone presents a compelling argument against leaving at all, he will go alone if his offer is turned down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T09:15:24-07:00","id":977207,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William quietly listened to his companions a slight smile crossing his lips, <b>&quot;It seems our skills are many and varied, most excellent, this bodes well for our chances of success.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> He stands from the chair regarding Raul, <b>&quot;Agreed, from what I remember last time I was through Nottingham we are expected to present ourselves to the Sheriff by the end of our first full night here. So the rest of tonight should be available for us to search the graveyard Mr. Abrantes, and of course anyone else interested may join us.&quot; </b><br /> <br /> <br /> At this point he puts on his coat and makes his way toward the door. <b>&quot;If there is nothing else I am off to the graveyard to make use of as much of the night as possible.&quot; </b>He pauses at the door in case someone else has something to interject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T04:33:57-07:00","id":977685,"title":"","content":"&quot;Well, If we must wait until tomorrow to make ourselves know anyway, I may join you in your midnight visit. I'm sure we could find some tasty morsels for tonight's dinner. I have a bottle of Jerez wine that would maridate perfectly with a dish of liver or kidneys.- he claps and smiles gigidly in anticipation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T17:28:22-07:00","id":978058,"title":"","content":"William and anyone else who goes with him reach the cemetery in less than 15 minutes walking. This time of night it is dark and deserted, the moonlight casting great shadows over the area from the ancient trees scattered across the cemetery grounds. An ancient crypt lies in the centre of the cemetery, presumably it is the location of where the meeting will take place. Despite not seeing another human or vampire while you are in the cemetery, you can't shake the feeling that you are being watched.<br /> <br /> <br /> [ooc]I am trying to balance giving you guys a chance to talk among yourselves while not letting things stagnate and interest being lost. Let me know if I am moving things ahead to fast or slow.[/ooc]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12161,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","user":"Browman","date":". 09-28-2016, 08:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T03:52:43-07:00","id":978301,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul remains unfazed by the eerie atmosphere of the place. As if it was the most normal thing to do he uses his Necromancy to percieve any ghosts that may lurk in the area*. Even if there are any, however, he first turns to the crypt in the middle, trying to find any odd details like mystical symbols or evidence of someone else tampering with the place. In the unlikely event that the crypt is freely accessible, he also checks inside**.<br /> <br /> Unless the search uncovers something disturbing, he finally turns to what he came for - disturbing the dead. Since he has no items useful in summoning on himself right now, he looks for graves of children, mindful that friends and relatives often leave at these sites exactly what he needs - toys, photos and the like. Of course, if more promising opportunity presents itself, he shall take it. If the search yields any degree of success, he goes right in for the summoning, using the Summon Soul power***. Anxiously, he awaits the answer.<br /> <br /> [OOC: That's a lot of rolls for one post. Let me know if I'm moving too fast or assuming too much and I will edit it]<br /> *A Perception+Awareness roll (dice pool 8 +1 specialization); 10,2,2,2,3,6,10 - this is 1 success<br /> **Perception+Alertness (dice pool 3); 3,2,8 - 1 success again<br /> ***Manipulation+Occult (9 dice) 3,10,2,6,1,9,5,3,6 - 1 success. Not my night, apparently. <br /> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Dice roller used</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-30T14:01:31-07:00","id":979253,"title":"","content":"Raul notices a single ghost that seems to be hovering around a specific grave. As he approaches he sees a small headstone that indicates it is the grave of a young man who died sometime last year, he was 21 or 22.<br /> <br /> Raul can see inside, but there is a grate over the entrance to the crypt. A large padlock holds the grate in place. From what you can see there is a single stone casket in the centre, you can't tell from here who it belongs to.<br /> <br /> He finds a small toy sitting on a headstone a few meters away. With it and the name on the Tomb stone, he summons the ghost of 5 year old Jimmy Anderson. <b>&quot;I'm cold.&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T00:57:21-07:00","id":979547,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William found the graveyard comforting and calming. Ever since his embrace graveyards have called to him, not just as a source of wraithly servants but some sort of deeper sensation he can't put his finger on. Initially following Raul he examines the center crypt, but being unable to make out the name and the padlock barring further progress he moves on to searching the rest of the graveyard.<br /> <br /> He settles on trying to peer beyond the Shroud and see if there is anything different compared to the living lands as well as look for any ghosts or other entities in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> [OOC: Shroudsight Perception + Awareness Difficulty 7: (Dice Pool 5): 7, 1, 8, 6, 1 - Failure]<br /> <br /> Finding it odd that he cannot see beyond the Shroud he finally notices the sensation of being observed which he had missed before due to the distraction of the graveyard. He begins looking around carefully trying see if he can figure out what the source of the sensation of being watched is coming from.<br /> <br /> [OOC: Looking for why he feels like he's being watched Perception + Alertness &lt;Unknown Difficulty&gt;: (Dice Pool 3): 5, 2, 5 (odds are this is a failure so I will continue on as such, if its not let me know and I will edit as necessary)]<br /> <br /> Unable to find the source of whatever was giving him the sense of being watched he assumes that its just irritation from his sight failing. He closes his eyes and takes a moment to focus on the stillness of the graveyard, the ethereal sensation he gets from them and decides to try seeing beyond the Shroud again.<br /> <br /> [OOC: Shroudsight Perception + Awareness Difficulty 8 (7 +1 From Trying it Again V20 pg 251): (Dice Pool 5, Spending a Willpower): 7, 1, 5, 8, 9 - 2 successes Shroudsight active for the scene]<br /> <br /> Centering himself and taking a moment seems to have cleared the cobwebs from his head and he is able to see into the Shroudlands and begins to search the graveyard now able to see into the lands of the dead. [OOC: Awaiting ST information about what I see beyond the Shroud]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Dice roller used</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T04:50:40-07:00","id":979593,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> After a long while of walking around, Raul concludes that there is nothing of note in this place - at least, nothing he can see. The crypt may yet hold something interesting, but until he can find someone that can pick the lock - like that Rosselini fellow - it is all moot anyway. &quot;No matter&quot; he thought to himself, as he appraises the young man's ghost. Not a longtime denizen of this cemetery, but still might know something useful. However, without his posession of some kind there is no guarantee that the ghost will answer truthfully, or that he will cooperate at all.<br /> <br /> The summoning rituall was straining and accompanied by the usual feeling of dread, but it was nonetheless successful - before him stood a spectral figure of a little boy, seemingly confused. Raul crouched to level his face with the boy's and spoke, his words dripping with sweet venom:<br /> <br /> - Easy, child. Everything is fine. Now, tell me what I need to know, so that you may return to your slumber.<br /> His eyes flared up for a moment, as he moved his left hand in an occult gesture and uttered a few words in Latin, compelling the ghost to obey.<br /> <br /> [OOC: Compel Soul is a contested roll and it allows me to issue orders of varying difficulty or ask 1-5 questions. I scored 8 successes [6,10,4,10,10,10,8,6,9], so unless the ghosts rolls 4 or more I get to ask 5 questions. These are the following:<br /> <br /> 1. Has anyone entered the cemetery after dark in recent weeks?<br /> 2. If yes, what did they look like? If no, what is the oldest ghost fettered in this graveyard?<br /> 3. Are there any hidden tunnels, chambers, stashes or anything of the sort in this graveyard?<br /> 4. Has he heard someone named &quot;Camden&quot; being discussed here recently?<br /> 5. What, if any, was the strangest occurence that happend here in the past week?<br /> <br /> If the number of my net successes is reduced below 5 and I have to choose, the questions are in order from most to least important]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Dice roller used</a><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T05:45:06-07:00","id":979612,"title":"","content":"Wallace enters the lichyard the last, holding a small portable fridge in one hand and a set of medical implements folded in a leather wrap inside his coat. <br /> He walks trough the place like in a supermarket, taking note of the decease dates, looking for something fresh. He is so into it that it takes him a while to realize they are apparently being watched. - &quot;Gentlemen...&quot; - he starts, but soon sees both of the necromancers with their sight focused elsewhere and one of them kneeling and speaking alone. - &quot;... nevermind&quot; - he coughs twice and keeps searching for dinner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 10-01-2016, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T12:51:46-07:00","id":980955,"title":"","content":"<i>-Alfie would sigh if he could sitting in the driver's seat of the rental car outside the Cemetary as he leans back and keeps an eye out while watching a show on his phone.-</i><br /> <br /> Perception+Alertness Proactively to notice anything out of the ordinary and Trying not to draw attention to being in a car near a Cemetary after dark. Stealth + Dexterity. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\" style=\"background-color: #151515\"><td width=\"101\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\">2016-10-03 13:47:20</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Alfie</span> rolls 4 dice to <span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Casual Observation</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:red\">9,10,5,3<span style=\"color:CCCCCC\"><b> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/?show_roll=581119\" target=\"_blank\">[2 successes]</a></b></span></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\" style=\"background-color: #151515\"><td width=\"101\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\">2016-10-03 13:49:58</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Aflie Rossellini</span> rolls 5 dice to <span style=\"color:#99CCCC\">Keeping a Low Profile</span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px\"><span style=\"color:red\">5,8,3,4,8<span style=\"color:CCCCCC\"><b> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/?show_roll=581120\" target=\"_blank\">[2 successes]</a></b></span></span></td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12246-avalon2099","name":"Avalon2099","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12246_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:27:48-07:00","id":981725,"title":"","content":"While the new team member keeps a low profile, he notices that an owl appears to be keeping an eye on the group.<br /> <br /> Wallace sees a fresh grave, it is max two days old, a man in his late 40s.<br /> <br /> William sees the same ghost that Raul noticed in addition to the one he summoned.<br /> <br /> As for Raul's questions<br /> <b>Only animals, an owl lives in the crypt. No old ghosts here. No, No. You.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> [ooc]Sorry it took a few days, been busy[/ooc]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:07:39-07:00","id":983554,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul is disappointed by the ghost's response, to say the least. He waves his hand and the apparition disappears into thin air. With hands in the pockets of his coat, he starts to walk in the general direction of the gate. Anyone could see that he hoped that there was something - anything - of note in this damn place. Hell, even an immediate danger would be appreciated. As he passes by Dunsirn and St. John, he says:<br /> <br /> - Nothing. The place is clean and deserted. If anyone is looking for Camden's lair, he has not been here.<br /> <br /> As he leaves, he informs them that he will be by the gate &quot;in case someone needs me&quot;, but other than that he intends to just leave the area and rest. Nothing to do here.<br /> He hopes the news of the Nosferatu will be a bit more exciting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:28:47-07:00","id":983627,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> He nods to Raul <b>&quot;Perhaps, but there is another entity you have not questioned. Maybe he will know more than the child.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> William walks over to where the ghost in his 20's currently is and attempts to speak to him.<br /> <br /> [OOC] Ash Path 2 Lifeless Tongues (cost 1 willpower) Perception + Occult (pool 6 difficulty 6) (4,2,4,3,2,5) [/OOC]<br /> <br /> Seeing that the ghost doesnt seem to understand him, and cursing whatever foul luck seems to have afflicted him he gives it one more shot.<br /> <br /> [OOC] Ash Path 2 Lifeless Tongues (cost 1 willpower) Perception + Occult (pool 6 difficulty 7 trying it again) (6,10,8,4,8,2) [/OOC]<br /> <br /> It seems like anything will have to be done the hard way this evening he thought to himself as the ghost finally gave sign of recognition that it could understand him.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;You there, when was the last time you saw anyone travel through here other than us tonight and have you seen anyone...strange looking maybe deformed travel through here before</b>?<b> Has anyone entered the crypt in the center that you can remember?</b>&quot; He looks over briefly at the crypt in the center to give the ghost direction to what he refers to.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Dice roller used</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:59:29-07:00","id":983955,"title":"","content":"Wallace nods to Raul as he passes by and explains his findings. - &quot;Just a minute, if you do not mind. I found something prommising&quot;- he claws his big hands on the tomb and tries to open it by sheer force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:19:39-07:00","id":985759,"title":"","content":"The ghost william talks to seems helpful. <b>&quot;People no, but several animals have been entering. I didn't pay much attention, but several seemed big for their species.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Wallace opens the grate fairly easily, but if anyone looks closely they will be able to tell that it has been forced open. Inside the crypt, there is a stone coffin carved with a name and dates. David Jones Beckett 1886-1961.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T21:38:31-07:00","id":986573,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William walks over to where Raul is waiting by the gate. <b>&quot;The other ghost claims to have seen animals which seemed strange strangely large for their species. Could be a sign of ghouled animals perhaps combined with animalism both of which the Nosferatu are known for.&quot; </b><br /> <br /> He looks over the where Wallace is at the crypt, and notices the man has gotten the door open. <b>&quot;Excellent, it seems our companion has gained entrance to the crypt.&quot; </b>William heads over to the crypt and begins looking around inside, taking note of the coffin and its inscription.<br /> <br /> [OOC] Is there a roll William can make to see if he recognizes the name of the coffin. [/OOC]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T09:05:00-07:00","id":986793,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> The fact that the crypt's gate is now open and the thought about ghouled animals William has voiced got Raul thinking that their time here may not be a complete waste after all. As he followed William down the path and into the tomb, he thought that something doesn't quite add up.<br /> <br /> - Well, If I may, William... can I call you by name? Anyway, I don't think the ghost has seen ghouls. See, from my experience ghouls don't usually wander around without their masters, and the kid specifically said that no one resembling a human visited in quite some time. What,s more, if they are guard animals, like dogs... where are they? And scouting the place with stray cats is just too much of a hassle, especially for someone that can become nearly invisible at will.<br /> <br /> He slows down for a second, right before the crypt, growing expression of concern on his face.<br /> <br /> - I think there might be something strange afoot. Perhaps werewolfs? Or... other... things?<br /> <br /> As he enters the crypt he starts to examine the walls and any objects beside the actual sarcophagus. He doubts the name would tell him something, but maybe there are some things indicating who the man was in life. Out of professional curiosity, Raul searches for any occult symbols or masonic paraphernalia, just now noticing that they have broken in here without a clear reason.<br /> <br /> [OOC: Is there any roll to make to determine if I am actually right about the animals not being ghouls? I know I have no practical data at hand, but there can't be that many creatures that can turn into giant animals... right? On the other hand, various supernaturals don't usually mingle together, so all that Occult dots may be of limited use. Also, I made a 3-dice Perception roll with 1 success (3,3,6)][<a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">roll</a>]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":10396,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","user":"Woland","date":". 10-13-2016, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T15:50:40-07:00","id":986984,"title":"","content":"[ooc]recognizing the name is an Int+Academics or Investigation roll. For the Animals make an Int+Occult roll Diff 7[/ooc]<br /> <br /> <br /> Raul and William notices an odd number of bones and skulls in the symbols carved into the walls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T20:41:49-07:00","id":987082,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William starts looking around the crypt in case it might provide any clues as to why this place was chosen for the meeting. As he does he starts noticing among the carvings along the walls that there are lots of bones and skulls carved into the walls. <b>&quot;Interesting, there seems to be an inordinate number of bones and skulls carved into the walls even for a graveyard. Perhaps this trip will not be as fruitless as it initially seemed.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> As he continues looking around the crypt he continues to search his memory on the name David Jones Beckett when it finally comes to him.<br /> <br /> [OOC] Roll to recognize the name David Jones Beckett, Intelligence + Academics (dice pool 7): 3,7,1,9,8,2,7 (3 successes) [/OOC]<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Now I remember David Jones Beckett is&quot; </b>[OOC] Awaiting GM info on the name [/OOC]<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Dice roller used</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","user":"Cynic01","date":".  Forgot to include dice roller link 10-13-2016, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T07:14:42-07:00","id":987242,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> As Raul removes dust and dirt from the walls, he notices that the carvings on them ar far from random. In fact, they are carvings of bones and skulls, indicating that this person had a degree of necromantic knowledge... or a really weird fetish. Whether or not he possesed any actual mystical power remains a mystery. Raul wished he could talk to his ghost, but as before - no tokens useful in summoning. Maybe another time.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, he let his thoughts wander on the subject of the strange animals. This could've been vampires, although it remains unlikely. His guess was werewolves or some weird branch of mages (he's heard once that there are spellcasters out there able to shapeshift... or something). He summoned as much arcane knowledge as he could and focused...<br /> <br /> [OOC a <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">roll</a> was made, using 10 dice (4,4,8,9,4,5,10,10,3,10), with 5 successes]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T20:36:32-07:00","id":987582,"title":"","content":"William remembers a few things about the name, first it would seem that David Jones Beckett was a fairly well off businessman, local politician and minor nobility, having some kind of old family house south of the city, second is that some claim that Lord Camden's mortal name was Thomas Becket.<br /> <br /> Raul remembers hearing vague rumours that some mages can turn into animals, disturbing claims that werewolves have distant kin that can change into different animals and that nosferateu often ghoul animals, long term nosferateu ghouls tend to grow large and mutatedly ugly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T00:32:09-07:00","id":987655,"title":"","content":"While his companions inspect the insides of the crypt, Wallace puts himself to work. He gently puts the fridge by his side and unwraps the leather sheet containing a set of surprisingly clean scalpels. - &quot;My, my, I hope you died of cirrhosis, it is been a while since I had some good foie&quot;- he says smiling and licking his lips in anticipation. <br /> He opens the casket and takes the corpse out, undressing it slowly from the waist up. <br /> -&quot; Hmmmmmm&quot;-he inhales with his eyes closed, in estacsy-&quot;How good... &quot;-he caress the body's abdomen in a very innapropiate way, gropping his kidneys through the flesh-&quot;Just a cut... here and... there...&quot; - he starts to hum like a nursing rhyme while slicing the sides of the body to get to its internal organs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T01:51:56-07:00","id":987675,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Now I remember David Jones Beckett was a fairly well off businessman, local politician, and minor noble. He had an old family house in the south of the city, which might be something to look into at some point should our timetable permit. Additionally Lord Camden's mortal name was believed to be Thomas Beckett.&quot; </b>William runs his fingers along the carvings on bones and skulls along the crypt wall. <b> &quot;And considering the carvings, perhaps there is something to that, maybe this David Jones Beckett is related in some way. If we are lucky necromantic leanings run through the family.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> He smiles at the thought, <b>&quot;Perhaps this trip will be much more valuable than I thought.&quot; </b>He looks over at Wallace, but makes it clear he is addressing Raul as well <b>&quot;When you are finished with your work we should check the coffin and the crypt for any hidden latches, buttons, or levers just in case there is more to this crypt than meets the eye. Not saying there will be, but I can only hope this is but the tip of the iceberg as it were.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> [OOC] Perception + Investigation (dice pool 3) roll to search for hidden latches elsewhere in the crypt 2,8,1 [/OOC]<br /> <br /> He begins going over the crypt, but is distracted by the thoughts of even greater secrets that two necromancers worth of information could provide and isn't searching as well as he should be whispering to himself, <b>&quot;What necromantic secrets might you hold Mr. Beckett?&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Dice roller used</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:36:16-07:00","id":988337,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> The walls in this crypt were apparently bare, so Raul took to searching for any cracks or floor tiles that might contain an opening mechanism. The whole affair takes him a few minutes and is surprisingly hard, despite his pale fingers trracing along any curve that appears suspicious (whgich is a lot, given the age of the crypt and the proportionate number of false positives).<br /> <br /> [OOC: 1 success with 6 dice (2,5,3,10,4,2) Perception+Investigation. <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Roll</a>]<br /> <br /> His body may be hugging the floor and walls, but his mind is far away from here. As he realizes that there are mages and shapeshifters out there that would fit the description nicely, he searched his memory for any pieces of information that he might have read, heard or even learn firsthand from encounters with said groups. Raul was especially interested in the general scope of tricks they were able to pull and weaknesses that could be exploited.<br /> <br /> [OOC: I took the liberty of rolling Intelligence+Occult (10 dice) again and scored 5 successes (again). Please let me know if it's at all relevant (i.e. if there is even the smallest chance of getting accurate information). <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Roll</a>]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T17:47:45-07:00","id":989631,"title":"","content":"Raul's search didn't find anything indicating a secret compartment of any kind. But his mind wandered while doing the task, thinking for more details about what he knew about shapechanging, which was fairly extensive. Shapeshifting through magic is possible to change what creature you appear as each time you shift, though without specific effort a mage would normally appear the same. Most true shapeshifters can't change their appearance in an animal form as their animal form is as much a part of them as their human form. In both cases a vampire could probably only tell one from a mundane animal using disciplines.<br /> <br /> William finds nothing to note.<br /> <br /> Wallace meanwhile is too busy getting an evening snack to help with the investigation.<br /> <br /> Your other friend hasn't left the car yet. [ooc]If he even still around[/ooc]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:51:47-07:00","id":990081,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hmmmm?&quot;- he nods, but keeps his eyes on his work- &quot;Of course, gentlemen, let me finish here&quot; -he takes the liver and kidneys and puts them in the fridge. His hands and sleeves covered in coagulated blood. -&quot;Ok, let me take a look, perhaps I can find something by chance that you have overlooked&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/447715\" target=\"_blank\">http://orokos.com/roll/447715</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":".  EDIT: Added Roll 10-20-2016, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T15:50:01-07:00","id":990148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/962857-ic-a-cycle-unending?p=990081#post990081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hmmmm?&quot;- he nods, but keeps his eyes on his work- &quot;Of course, gentlemen, let me finish here&quot; -he takes the liver and kidneys and puts them in the fridge. His hands and sleeves covered in coagulated blood. -&quot;Ok, let me take a look, perhaps I can find something by chance that you have overlooked&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">OOC: What should I roll?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>perception investigation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:41:30-07:00","id":991509,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> Raul is far too busy devising strategies for dealing with their adversaries to actually care about the fact that his Dunsirn companion is basically desacrating a grave. As revolting as the act was, he had - *they* had - bigger problems. He walked right to the car waiting outside, placed himself at the backseat and asked Alfie, probably still staring in his cellphone.<br /> <br /> - Hey, Rosselini. You ever killed a werewolf before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T15:35:53-07:00","id":995830,"title":"","content":"Since it seems that nothing else can be gained from the cemetery, the group makes it's way back towards the motel.<br /> <br /> [ooc]Sorry, been a busy week. If no one has anything else for the first night in nottingham I will move things to the next night tomorrow.[/ooc]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T18:06:33-07:00","id":995890,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> Despite their search the crypt would yield no other secrets...disappointing, worse it simply left the question of Mr. Beckett's nature hanging in the air. At least the information about strangely large animals might save them the trouble of a nasty surprise later.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;While this trip wasn't entirely a waste since being forewarned of possible dangers is helpful. It remains to be seen if this particular Mr. Beckett is going to be of any further use. Either way tomorrow we will need to present ourselves to the Prince if we are careful and lucky we might be able to find out some useful information.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> [OOC] I'm good to move on since the Cemetery has given us any secrets it has. [/OOC]<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T23:19:05-07:00","id":995978,"title":"","content":"Wallace attempts at investigation are pitiful and inefective, he is clearly thinking more on his dinner than anything else. <br /> He apologizes and packs his things before going back to the car mumbling a song about the best parts of a corpse and the proper order of consumption. <br /> <br /> (OOC: Yeah, let's move on to the next night)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T19:25:11-07:00","id":997504,"title":"","content":"The rest of the night and the next day pass uneventfully. You wake up in the motel without any issues.<br /> <br /> You know that you need to present yourselves at the club to not violate the rules the Prince of Nottingham and that you must do so an hour after dark.<br /> <br /> When you get to the club, it is basically empty as it is still quiet early. A man in his early middle ages with a bulky build and slightly receding hairline is sitting at the bar, a drink in front of him that doesn't look like it has been touched.<br /> <br /> The club looks like the kind of place that fills up on most nights, once it gets late enough at night. It would probably be an excellent place to feed. It could probably hold about 150 people at max capacity.<br /> <br /> The bartender is a woman in her late 20s or early 30s, and is basically completely forgettable. Which seems out of place for such a trendy club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:22:14-07:00","id":997907,"title":"","content":"Raul Abrantes<br /> <br /> The loud, brutish music that flooded the world as they entered irritated Raul. In fact, this whole situation of being between a herd of people and a Prince of whom he didn't know one thing made him want to leave as soon as possible and get to som real work, like further research or working future occult contacts. <br /> <br /> Nonetheless, he casually approaches the bartender, sits at one of the stools and orders a round of tequila. He gives a side eye to the stranger beside him and says to the woman:<br /> <br /> - Nice establishment you have here. I just came to town and I was wondering if you could amuse me with some of the latest gossip. I am particularly interested in anything on the... occultish side. Weird cults, mad prophets, creepy necromancers... yes, they are very exciting in their own way. But only legitimate. Trust me, darling, I may be a tourist but I am not stupid.<br /> <br /> He gives the barmaid a serious look, showing that he means business and won't fool around. He is polite, but insistent. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10396-woland","name":"Woland","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10396_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T10:47:38-08:00","id":999812,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;There is some sort of new age store in the Mall, probably best to try your luck there.&quot;</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:56:53-08:00","id":999930,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> William looked around the club, unfortunately not immediately noticing the Prince or Sheriff. The bartender caught his attention, specifically because of how much she didnt. Normally places like this hired pretty young things or large intimidating bruisers, so to have someone so forgettable was off. Raul had decided to approach the bartender and chat them up through the tourist route, something William couldnt do so he decided to let him have at it.<br /> <br /> He decided to take a seat at the far end of the bar so as to give him a good vantage point of most of the club, so he could hopefully notice when the Prince showed so they could present and move on to their own business without that deadline over their heads.<br /> <br /> As he sat there he noticed the bulky man wasnt touching his drink, was it acting as a cover or was he just nursing it? William looks the man over to see if he could notice the subtle traits of vampirism.<br /> <br /> [OOC]Roll to notice supernatural Perception + Awareness (Unknown Difficulty Dice Pool 5) - 4, 4, 1, 1, 9 (failure)[/OOC]<br /> <br /> After looking over the man for a moment he doesnt see the tell tale signs of vampirism and moves on before he gets caught staring. For the moment it seems the best course would be to wait for Prince to get that hassle out of the way.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/wod/\" target=\"_blank\">Dice roller used</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:53:21-08:00","id":999961,"title":"","content":"Wallace was on a pretty good mood. The liver and kidneys he had acquired yesterday made for an excellent meal, he wondered if something fresher would be even tastier as he caroused his way through the club. He payed some rounds here, made some jokes there, and in general mingled and made sure to make himslef noticeable. If Budha doesn't go to the mountain... well, he always prefered to attract the attention when he could afford it. Better for the flies to come to the spider.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Carousing: Charisma + Etiquette (Dif. 6) =<a href=\"http://orokos.com/roll/454330\" target=\"_blank\">4 Successes!</a></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He enjoys the attention and starts to look for an appetizer while his companions do their own thing. Ra\u00fal seems to have started pretty strong, who asks for actual necromancers on a bar? It kills the mood. William on the other hands seems to be getting the right idea, looking for a comfy corner where to take a look at the menu. Let's take the party to him.<br /> <br /> Wallace and his new friends, carrying asorted beberages sit next to him.<br /> <br /> -<b>&quot;William, my friend, I brought you something <i>to drink</i>&quot;</b>-he remarks with a naughty wink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-07-2016, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T19:48:48-08:00","id":1001157,"title":"","content":"Wallace makes friends with a pair of locals who enter the bar shortly after the group did. They work at an old factory on the south side of town, tough times have cut the shift back to 1 a day rather than running night and day.<br /> <br /> Within about 20 minutes of you arriving the bar begins to fill up. You notice a pair of people standing out, they are both wearing what look like stylish lab coats. They seem to be keeping an eye out for someone. They are talking in a language that you are pretty sure is German.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12161-browman","name":"Browman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T22:09:20-08:00","id":1001193,"title":"","content":"William St. John<br /> <br /> He notices the the twins in the lab coats although he can't quite make out what they are saying, from the bits he can pick out it probably wouldnt do any good even if he could since he had no knowledge of German. He makes a note to look into them later if possible since their dress and demeanor is so out of place, perhaps other buyers?<br /> <br /> He sees Wallace approach with a couple of people in tow and a tray of drinks. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>&quot;William, my friend, I brought you something <i>to drink</i>&quot;</b>-he remarks with a naughty wink. </div> </div> </div> Deciding to play along a little while also pointing out the odd ones, he replies rolling his eyes in an exaggerated way toward the twins that unless someone was following would take as jovial exasperation <b>&quot;Wallace you know I have business tomorrow and cant indulge like I would want. So in the meantime please introduce me to your new friends.&quot; </b>As they sit he takes a drink, but sets it down and occasionally looking like he's sipping at it like he's nursing it while looking like he is more interested in the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2008-cynic01","name":"Cynic01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"437"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}